From 79660c37156b9b5799a7099cd24b2dc94352bb2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:43:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 75/75] cellJpgEnc: the SDK's encoder, and rendered pixels
 written back for it

cellJpgEnc was a placeholder with made-up functions. Now QueryAttr, Open,
OpenEx, WaitForInput, EncodePicture/EncodePicture2, WaitForOutput,
GetStreamInfo, Reset and Close, with the structures laid out as 3D Dot Game
Heroes fills them: a grayscale, RGB, RGBA or ARGB picture is encoded at
once (stb_image_write) at the title's quality into a file (a /dev_hdd0 or
/dev_hdd1 path) or a guest buffer, and described by GetStreamInfo.

The title's SNAPSHOT encodes its display buffer, which the draw engine
renders on the host GPU: guest memory there held zeros, so the picture was
black. cellGcm_guest_read_surface writes the engine's pixels of a guest
rectangle back first (rsx_draw_engine_guest_read, as a 2D transfer reading
it does, under the FIFO walker's lock); the encoder calls it for a 32-bit
picture. The snapshot now shows the scene with the game's copyright line.
